,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.170932922918365,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.12502839354234907,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.242914979757085,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.25466,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Arcus Biosciences, Inc., a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company, develops and commercializes cancer therapies in the United States. The company's development product portfolio includes Casdatifan, a HIF-2a inhibitor for the treatment of kidney cancer; Domvanalimab, an anti-TIGIT antibody, which is in Phase 2 and Phase 3 clinical trial for lung and gastrointestinal cancers; and Zimberelimab, an anti-PD-1 antibody. It also develops Quemliclustat, a small molecule inhibitor that targets the CD73 enzyme in the ATP-adenosine pathway, which is in phase 3 and phase 1/1b clinical trial for lung and pancreatic cancer. In addition, the company develops AB598, a CD39 antibody, which is in phase 1/1b clinical study for gastrointestinal cancer and AB801, an AXL inhibitor, which is in Phase 1b clinical trial for lung cancer. It has clinical collaboration with AstraZeneca for the Phase 3 PACIFIC-8 trial evaluating domvanalimab and durvalumab in Stage 3 NSCLC and for a Phase 1/1b study evaluating casdatifan and volrustomig in IO-naive patients with ccRCC; BVF Partners L.P. to support the discovery and development of compounds for the treatment of inflammatory diseases; and Bristol-Myers Squibb Company to develop a novel treatment regimen that delivers tumor control in kidney cancer. Arcus Biosciences, Inc. was incorporated in 2015 and is based in Hayward, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Terry J. Rosen Ph.D. | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 601 people. Revenue per employee of $411K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 62%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $100K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Arcus Biosciences, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.5B market cap on $247M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +30% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -36% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $484M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +11.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -48.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 17.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 24% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 25% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +11.3% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash syst